{% doc %}
  Size chart for the Supreme Leader (SL) tees, shown on the product page directly
  under the description.

  Rendered from the `size_chart` custom_liquid block in templates/product.json
  (main-product block_order: ... description, size_chart, share). product.json is
  shared by EVERY product, so the gate lives here:
    - shown on every product whose handle starts with 'sl-'
    - ALSO shown on any product tagged 'size-chart' (future shirts on the same
      blanks that do not use the sl- prefix)
    - NEVER on a product tagged 'no-size-chart' (a piece on a different blank);
      the opt-out wins
  Everything else renders nothing.

  The image is the owner's chart (assets/ak-size-chart.jpg, 1200x1200, resized from
  the 2400px original). The same numbers are repeated in a visually hidden table so
  screen readers get the measurements, not a picture of text.

  Push order: assets/ak-size-chart.jpg + this snippet FIRST, templates/product.json
  SECOND. The render call runs for every product, so a missing snippet would print
  a Liquid error on every product page.

  @param {product} product - The product being viewed
  @example
    {% render 'ak-drop-size-chart', product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  Tags are compared lower-cased, element by element (array `contains` is an
  exact match), so 'No-Size-Chart' works and 'size-chart' never matches
  'no-size-chart'. The opt-out wins over the opt-in.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ak_show_size_chart = false
  assign ak_handle_prefix = product.handle | slice: 0, 3
  if ak_handle_prefix == 'sl-'
    assign ak_show_size_chart = true
  endif
  assign ak_tags = product.tags | join: '|' | downcase | split: '|'
  if ak_tags contains 'size-chart'
    assign ak_show_size_chart = true
  endif
  if ak_tags contains 'no-size-chart'
    assign ak_show_size_chart = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if ak_show_size_chart -%}
  <div class="ak-size-chart quick-add-hidden">
    <img
      class="ak-size-chart__img"
      src="{{ 'ak-size-chart.jpg' | asset_url }}"
      width="1200"
      height="1200"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="low"
      alt="AmeriKid T-shirt size chart"
    >
    <div class="visually-hidden">
      <table>
        <caption>AmeriKid T-shirt measurements in inches. Shirts conform to these measurements after the first wash.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Size</th><th scope="col">Pit to pit</th><th scope="col">Length</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Small</th><td>18.5</td><td>27</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Medium</th><td>20</td><td>28</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Large</th><td>21</td><td>30</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">XL</th><td>22.5</td><td>31</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- style -%}
    .ak-size-chart{ margin-top:2.4rem; }
    .ak-size-chart__img{ display:block;width:100%;max-width:56rem;height:auto; }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}
